# PtSwitch — Project context

**Full product spec:** [docs/PRD.md](docs/PRD.md)

## What this project does

- For each workout: goes **first** to the **access-token URL** (`https://medbridgego.com/access_token/$TOKEN`); does not authenticate at medbridgego.com beforehand. When that page prompts for login, authenticates with username/password, then scrapes.
- **Scrapes** one program per token (list of exercises: names, descriptions, sets/reps; no videos in MVP).
- **Generates a static site** with a top nav to switch between programs; run via `npm run scrape`.

## Tech stack

- **Runtime:** Node.js
- **Scraping:** Playwright (browser automation)
- **Config:** `.env` (see `.env.example`); `.env` is gitignored
- **Output:** Static HTML/CSS/JS only (e.g. `dist/` or `output/`), no server required to view

## Conventions

- **Env format:** `MEDBRIDGE_USERNAME`, `MEDBRIDGE_PASSWORD`; token/name pairs as `TOKEN_1`/`NAME_1`, `TOKEN_2`/`NAME_2`, etc.
- **Multi-token required:** MVP must support ≥2 tokens and verify that workouts differ per token.
- **Failure handling:** Run all tokens; use successful ones; clearly mark failed tokens (e.g. "Program name – failed to load") in the generated site.

## Constraints (MVP)

- No videos or image media in scraped output.
- No UI for token management — edit `.env` manually.
- Trigger: `npm run scrape` only (no regenerate button or scheduler in MVP).

When changing behavior or scope, align with [docs/PRD.md](docs/PRD.md) and update the PRD if requirements change.
